<title>MALAYSIA: Telekom offers employees 10pct stake.</title>
<headline>Telekom offers employees 10pct stake.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telekom Malaysia Bhd said on Wednesday it has planned an employees' share option scheme (ESOS) of up to 10 percent of its existing issued and paid-up share capital.</p>
<p>The share scheme will be in force for five years, Telekom said in a statement to the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The scheme will benefit employees who did not participate in a similar exercise in 1991, which expired on Dec 11 this year, the company added.</p>
<p>It said the issue would not have any immediate effect on the existing equity content of Telekom, although changes were expected progressively depending on the number of options exercised in the ESOS.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-2307509)</p>
</text>
